class Solution {
    public int ladderLength(String beginWord, String endWord, List<String> wordList) {
        Set<String> set = new HashSet<>(wordList);
        if(! set.contains(endWord))
            return 0;
        set.add(beginWord);

        Queue<String> queue = new LinkedList<>();
        queue.offer(beginWord);

        int level = 0;

        while(! queue.isEmpty()){
            int size = queue.size();
            for(int i=0; i < size; i++){
                String curr = queue.poll();
                if(curr.equals(endWord))
                   return level+1;
                for(String child : getNeighbors(curr, set)){
                   queue.offer(child);
                }
            }
            level++;
        }
        return 0;
    }
    private List<String> getNeighbors(String curr, Set<String> set){
        List<String> neighbors = new ArrayList<>();
        for(int i=0; i < curr.length(); i++){    // O(L)
            char arr[] = curr.toCharArray();     // O(L)
            for(char ch='a'; ch <= 'z'; ch++){
                arr[i] = ch;
                String word = String.valueOf(arr);    // O(L)
                if(set.remove(word) && ! word.equals(curr)){
                    neighbors.add(word);
                }
            }
        }
        System.out.println("word " + curr + "  neigbors " + neighbors.toString());
        return neighbors;
    }
}

Time : O(n*L2)
for every word, it is taking L*L time to get neighbors.
O(n * L * O(L + 26 * L))
O(n * L2)

Space : O(n)

We don’t count memory that is created and destroyed immediately inside each iteration.
The neighbors list is temporary, exists only inside the function call, and is garbage-collected after returning.
So we only count the peak memory usage at any moment, not the total over the whole run.

For each word in BFS:
You create a new temporary list of size at most 26 * L
You add a bunch of neighbor strings
You return the list → BFS iterates over it
After BFS processes it, that list becomes unreachable → garbage collected
So at any moment:
Only one neighbors list exists
Not one per word simultaneously
